    "shortDescription": "Reported Android interview question for mid-level candidates.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Kotlin structured concurrency means coroutines are organized in\na hierarchy of scopes so their lifetimes, cancellation, and failures are\npredictable. A parent scope owns its child coroutines; when the parent\nis cancelled, children are cancelled.\n\nAndroid commonly uses viewModelScope and lifecycleScope so work is tied\nto a lifecycle owner. Structured concurrency prevents orphaned\nbackground work and makes cancellation easier to reason about.\ncoroutineScope propagates child failure, while supervisorScope isolates\nsibling failures.",
