    "shortDescription": "Reported Android interview question for senior / advanced candidates.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Compose commonly follows unidirectional data flow. State is\nowned by a state holder such as a ViewModel, the UI observes that state,\nand user actions are sent back as events. The state owner processes the\nevent and emits updated state, which causes the relevant UI to\nrecompose.\n\nThis approach makes state changes easier to trace and test. It also\ndiscourages hidden mutable state spread across multiple Composables.",
